| Count | Value | Note |
|---|---:|---|
| Alerts in scope | 160 | |
| Published library risks with text | 116 | The direct lane's candidate pool |
| Library risks with **any** RSM parent in the mapping extract | ~85 | The routed lane's structural ceiling |
| Distinct library risks the routed lane actually offered | 62 | Across all 160 alerts |
| Distinct library risks appearing in the golden (in scope) | 49 | |
| Golden Record → Library Risk pairs in scope | 1,229 | |
| `risk_text` length — median / min / max | 3,754 / 333 / 5,345 | characters |
| Risks flagged `(TO BE RETIRED)` still in the pool | 28 | 24% of the candidate set |

**Two coverage findings worth carrying forward:**

1. Only ~85 of 116 published library risks have any Regulation Summary parent. Roughly **31 published risks are structurally unreachable by the routed lane** — not narrowly reached, unreachable, for any alert, ever.
2. For these 160 alerts the routed lane ever offered the model **62 of 116** risks. Fifty-four were never a candidate for any alert in scope.

Separately, only 49 distinct risks appear anywhere in the golden for these alerts. The other 67 have no golden link at all, so every prediction against them lands in the discovery bucket by construction.

