## 6. Results — direct lane (Direct Iteration 1)

### 6.1 Run

18,560 pairs · 480 model calls · 8m46s · 0 call errors · all `finish_reason: stop`

### 6.2 Head-to-head, same golden, same 1,229 denominator

| Metric | Routed | Direct | Δ |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Validated (caught) | 258 | 273 | **+15** |
| Judged not linked | 831 | 922 | +91 |
| Judged error | 9 | 34 | +25 |
| Never judged | 131 | **0** | −131 |
| Addressable denominator | 1,229 | 1,229 | 0 |
| Discoveries | 159 | 1,357 | +1,198 |
| Pairs judged | 2,409 | 18,560 | +16,151 |
| **Addressable recall** | **21.0%** | **22.2%** | **+1.2 pts** |

*(routed-lane figures here are the rescored set — see §8.3)*

### 6.3 Confusion matrix (18,560 judged pairs)

| | Golden linked | Golden not linked | Total |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Model LINKED | 273 | 1,357 | 1,630 |
| Model NOT LINKED | 956 | 15,974 | 16,930 |
| **Total** | **1,229** | **17,331** | **18,560** |

FN 956 = 922 declined + 34 errored. Never judged = 0.

### 6.4 Discovery rate

| | Routed | Direct |
|---|---:|---:|
| Non-golden pairs judged | 1,311 | 17,331 |
| Discoveries | 165 | 1,357 |
| **Discovery rate** | **12.6%** | **7.8%** |

Volume rose ~8×; the rate **fell**. The extra discoveries come from judging more pairs, not from better targeting.

### 6.5 What the experiment concluded

- The 131 golden links the route hid were worth about **fifteen** real catches, not 131. The upstream RSM gap was real but far smaller than assumed. **This closes the "upstream recall is the ceiling" hypothesis.**
- `NOT_JUDGED = 0`. In the routed lane a miss could be a model decision **or** a routing gap and the two could not be separated. In the direct lane every miss is a model decision. **This is the main win** — it is what makes a miss audit interpretable.
- +1.2 pts of recall for 7.7× the pairs judged is not, on its own, a case for adopting the direct lane. The clean audit frame is.

