## 8. Known issues and open risks

### 8.1 The over-mapping split is audit-derived, not arithmetic — MEDIUM

The 707 / 119 split comes from an LLM audit that is **told the over-mapping hypothesis** and is **shown whether the golden says linked**. It returns near-zero model fault whichever way the model performs (2 in v0, 1 in v1 despite +119 caught links). It is corroborating evidence, not independent proof.

**Mitigation in flight:** a deterministic reachability test — for each miss, was the risk reachable through a *specifically linked* summary, or only through the whole-regulation sweep? No LLM in the loop. This converts the 93% from an assertion into an audited fact.

### 8.2 The direct lane has no usable audit — HIGH

The same audit run against the direct lane's 956 misses returned a **single category — "text too thin" — at 100%, with zero model fault**, against risk text averaging 3,754 characters (minimum 333). A classifier putting every case in one bucket is not discriminating, and it contradicts the routed lane's audit on the same golden.

**Consequence:** there is no text-derivable recall figure for the direct lane. The 93% must be presented as a **routed-lane number only**.

**Action:** read the raw reasoning on a sample of `audited` rows — the symptom looks like an empty or truncated payload reaching the auditor, not a judgement.

### 8.3 Two routed-lane scorecards disagree — MEDIUM

The same verdicts parquet scored by two versions of the scorecard:

| Gate | Original | Rescored | Δ |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Caught | 253 | 258 | +5 |
| Judged not linked | 845 | 831 | −14 |
| Judged error | 0 | 9 | +9 |
| Never judged | 131 | 131 | 0 |
| Discoveries | 165 | 159 | −6 |
| Addressable recall | 20.6% | 21.0% | +0.4 pts |

**Cause:** duplicate `(RECORD_ID, LIB_RISK)` rows with conflicting verdicts, resolved in opposite directions; plus omitted-id rows broken out as their own gate rather than folded into "not linked". Both sum to 1,229, so neither is arithmetically wrong.

**Action:** count the duplicates, adopt one scorecard for both lanes, quote one per document.

### 8.4 28 risks flagged for retirement are still in the pool — MEDIUM

24% of the candidate set is marked `(TO BE RETIRED)` but still passes the Published filter. They inflate the denominator and generate discoveries nobody wants. A data fix, no model change.

### 8.5 Discovery value is unproven — MEDIUM

No SME has reviewed the candidate links. Until a sample is validated, discoveries are a **volume, not a benefit**. 1,357 is beyond what an SME will review — rank by `relevance_score` and take a top slice.

### 8.6 Omitted-id rows — LOW

34 of 18,560 pairs (0.2%) came back with the risk id absent from the response. They are counted as misses, which is the conservative treatment. The row-per-candidate loop catches these rather than letting the pair vanish. Not currently a concern at chunk size 40.

