## 12. Reporting guidance

Things that will be asked, and the honest answer:

**"Why is recall only 22%?"** — Because the golden's denominator contains links no reader of the two texts would make. Against text-derivable truth it is 93% in the routed lane. That figure is currently audit-derived and being converted to arithmetic.

**"How do you know the 707 aren't real misses?"** — We do not, with certainty. The audit says so, but the audit is not independent. The reachability test in §9.1 is what will settle it. *(This is the single question that can unravel the 93%. Pre-empt it.)*

**"What did removing the route buy?"** — About fifteen more validated links and, more importantly, a clean audit frame: every miss is now a model decision rather than a routing artefact.

**"Are the 1,357 discoveries real?"** — Unknown. No SME has reviewed them. The discovery *rate* per pair judged actually fell.

**Never report precision or F1.** The golden is non-exhaustive; a false positive here is a candidate link, not an error.
